9-walkers-london-transport-2.jpg","c":"Bert East (centre) had difficulty in even making the start of the London Transport '2' on July 6th at Acton, but mention the word \"handicap\" and he's off like a shot! Ray Middleton thinks it's a laugh beating the 2 miles record of a No.11 bus, while Wil Wesch gets on with winning at well over speed-limit","id":"B171-18","w":"September 1969"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B171/B171-p09-walkers-london-transport-2.jpg","caption":"Bert East (centre) had difficulty in even making the start of the London Transport '2' on July 6th at Acton, but mention the word \"handicap\" and he's off like a shot! Ray Middleton thinks it's a laugh beating the 2 miles record of a No.11 bus, while Wil Wesch gets on with winning at well over speed-limit","source":"B171-18","when":"September 1969"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"Bert East in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1925–1977: 326 mentions in 125 issues, 239 race results and 1 photograph.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B171/B171-p09-walkers-london-transport-2.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-bert-east.html"},"legend":false}